diff --git a/docs/harness/log.md b/docs/harness/log.md
index f53d2fc6e..31e208ff6 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -110,3 +110,22 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - ci: npx -y uw-harness verify returned 404 from the npm registry on 2026-11-01 (package not published). The new harness.yml workflow will fail until uw-harness is published; it was not run on GitHub. Locally the check was run with the uw-harness source checkout and passed.
 - local-env: PostgreSQL support (DB_TYPE=pgsql, compose profile pgsql) was written but not run. Only MySQL was verified. The full gate drops and reinstalls the local database each time, and needs host port 3306 free because the mysqli driver ignores other ports.
 - full-gate: The full gate does not build the DocBook guides or the SOAP WSDL HTML (documentation.yml needs Publican and xsltproc, not available as composer/npm dependencies). Everything else from CI (lint, api:validate, api:generate, all four PHPUnit suites) is in composer run check.
+
+## 2026-11-01: Category handler as a user reference (issue #32470)
+
+**Changed**
+
+- `CategoryAddCommand` and `CategoryUpdateCommand` take `handler` (`{"id": n}` or `{"name": "x"}`) instead of the integer `assigned_to`. On update, a missing `handler` keeps the current one and `"handler": null` clears it. New helper `category_handler_to_user_id()` in `core/category_api.php`.
+- `CategoryGetCommand` returns `handler` instead of `default_handler`.
+- Callers updated: SOAP `mc_project_rename_category_by_name()`, `manage_proj_cat_update.php`, `manage_proj_cat_edit_page.php`, `manage_proj_page.php`, `manage_proj_edit_page.php`. OpenAPI request schemas and GET descriptions updated.
+- Tests: `tests/Mantis/CategoryCommandTest.php`, `tests/rest/RestProjectCategoryTest.php`.
+
+**Learned**
+
+- `Command::payload()` uses `isset()`, so it cannot tell a missing key from an explicit `null`. Use `array_key_exists( 'x', $this->data['payload'] )` when `null` has a meaning.
+- After `composer run check` the PHP web server is stopped. To run the `rest` or `soap` tests alone afterwards, start `build/local_instance.sh serve` again.
+- redocly rule `nullable-type-sibling`: a `nullable: true` property with `allOf` also needs `type: object`.
+
+**Left**
+
+- The old `assigned_to` request field is no longer read (it is ignored, not rejected). If REST clients of a released version use it, a deprecation path may be needed.
